  <prompt>Create two new Multiple-lines-of-text (memo) columns on `sprk_communication`, packed into the managed solution (ADR-027): `sprk_deliveredmailboxes` (a `"; "`-delimited SET-UNION of the monitored-mailbox addresses that delivered a copy of this email) and `sprk_savedbyusers` (a set-union of the user identities that saved a copy via upload). These are the storage the task-022 FR-C2 context-merge code (already merged — `DeliveryContextMerge` + `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` + `OfficeDocumentPersistence`) reads + writes.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Dataverse schema expertise. Use `dataverse-create-schema` (Web API + PowerShell — no `pac column create`). Follow ADR-027 strictly.</role>
  <goal>Two memo columns `sprk_communication.sprk_deliveredmailboxes` + `sprk_savedbyusers` exist, published, carried in the managed solution; verified in `spaarkedev1` (a value round-trips). The task-022 code then records the full delivery/uploader set on the canonical row end-to-end.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Task 022 (FR-C2) implemented the context-merge in CODE (merged): on a dedup reconcile, the delivering mailbox is merged onto the canonical row's `sprk_deliveredmailboxes` (set-union, idempotent, non-fatal), and on an email upload the saver is merged onto `sprk_savedbyusers`. ALL that code ships behind these two columns: every write goes through the non-fatal `DeliveryContextMerge.MergeAsync` (NOT the atomic entity build), so capture/upload never fails on the columns being absent before this gated deploy — this is the ENABLEMENT step, not a blocker to the code merge. See `notes/022-context-merge-on-duplicate-complete.md`. Mechanism mirrors task 023/027 exactly.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/tasks/027-canonicaldocument-selflookup-schema.poml (sibling gated schema task — same recipe)</file>
      <file role="reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/DeliveryContextMerge.cs (the reader/writer + the two attribute-name constants)</file>
      <file role="modify">Dataverse managed solution — sprk_communication entity metadata</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: two Multiple-lines-of-text (memo) columns — `sprk_deliveredmailboxes` + `sprk_savedbyusers`. Nullable (empty until the first merge). Sufficient length for a set of addresses (memo default is ample; the code bounds at 8000 chars).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Author into the managed solution + export so it deploys to every subscription; do NOT create unmanaged in one environment.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: schema mechanism. Use `dataverse-create-schema` (Web API + PowerShell); PAC CLI has no column-create path here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: GATED on operator go-ahead (mutates live Dataverse schema in `spaarkedev1`). Do NOT run autonomously.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Dataverse memo columns for de-duplication delivery-context set-union</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-027-subscription-isolation-and-dataverse-solution-management.md</file>
