    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load POML + task-022 completion note + ADR-027. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: STANDARD. Confirm operator go-ahead. Invoke dataverse-create-schema.</step>
    <step order="1">Create the two memo columns via the skill; poll to Active.</step>
    <step order="2">Add them to the managed solution; export; verify both are in the export.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify in `spaarkedev1`: a `"; "`-delimited value round-trips on both columns; the task-022 code records the set end-to-end (dedup a message across two mailboxes → the canonical lists both).</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="5">Document any deviation in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>No field on `sprk_communication` accumulates a SET of delivering mailboxes or savers: `sprk_to`/`sprk_cc` are the email's recipients (identical across copies of one email); `sprk_communicationaccount` is a separate entity (mailbox config); a lookup holds ONE value, not a set.</existing>
    <extension>No — reusing recipient fields corrupts their semantics (recipients ≠ delivering mailboxes); a lookup can't hold N; a child entity is discouraged (ADR-045 extend-not-fork; the canonical row stays the reconciliation unit). Two additive memo set-columns ARE the extension.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without these columns the task-022 merge has nowhere to record the discarded copies' context: on dedup, the fact that mailboxes B/C also received the email — and that user X also saved it — is DROPPED (FR-C2's core failure). Downstream review can't see the full delivery picture.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dataverse-create-schema">Create the two memo columns via Web API + PowerShell</tool>
    <tool name="pwsh">Solution export</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="schema">Two memo columns sprk_communication.sprk_deliveredmailboxes + sprk_savedbyusers</output>
    <output type="solution">Managed solution export containing both columns</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the deployed schema, when queried, then both `sprk_deliveredmailboxes` and `sprk_savedbyusers` exist as Multiple-lines-of-text on `sprk_communication` and are nullable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the managed solution export, when inspected, then both column definitions are present (deploy to every subscription per ADR-027).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `sprk_communication` row in `spaarkedev1`, when a `"; "`-delimited value is written to each column and read back, then it round-trips.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">End-to-end: dedup the same email across two monitored mailboxes → the canonical row's `sprk_deliveredmailboxes` lists BOTH (task-022 code + these columns).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-C2 "no delivery fact lost". Enables the task-022 code (merged) end-to-end. Sibling of task 023/027 (schema-c). GATED on operator go-ahead. Forward-only (pre-existing rows stay null until their next dedup touch).</notes>

